        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e90adad4-01bc-5dc0-8508-cc87b2919eab",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sheridan County, Montana; Chandra Taal; Suraj Tal; Plentywood; Himachal Pradesh; Spiti; Lahul and Spiti district\n- Products/Systems: Sher-Wood Airport; IATA PWD; ICAO KPWD; FAA LID PWD\n- Concepts: Chandra River; Chandrabhaga; Lake of the Moon\n\nFacts:\n- Sheridan County is a county in the U.S. state of Montana.\n- Chandra Taal, meaning \"Lake of the Moon,\" is also called Chandra Tal and is in the Spiti part of Lahul and Spiti district in Himachal Pradesh, India.\n- Sher-Wood Airport is a public-use airport located 1 nautical mile northeast of the central business district of Plentywood in Sheridan County, Montana, United States.\n- Sher-Wood Airport has the codes IATA PWD, ICAO KPWD, and FAA LID PWD.\n- The Chandra River, a major tributary of the Chandrabhaga, originates from a glacier near Chandra Taal lake in the Spiti district.",
